titled “Accuracy of Petroleum Supply Data” available at: http://www.        big-box and non-big-box outlets. Big-box outlets typically sell large\n eia.doe.gov/petroleum/supply/monthly/ archive/2009/2009_02/pdf/               volumes of gasoline at discounted prices.\n art0902.pdf\n                                                                               The EIA-878 sample was drawn from a frame of approximately\n                                                                               130,000 retail gasoline outlets in the United States that were active in\n                                                                               2016. The gasoline outlet frame was constructed by combining outlet\n Confidentiality—Data protection and disclosure -                              information from a private commercial source with information\n                                                                               contained on existing EIA petroleum product frames and surveys,\n Weekly Supply Surveys                                                         federal and state administrative records, and other publicly available\n                                                                               sources. Outlet names, physical addresses, and ZIP codes were\n\n\n\n\n40                                              Weekly Petroleum Status Report/Energy Information Administration",
